" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134294137,imgsize-97511.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Syria's parliament votes to scrap Assad-era terrorism court, nullify rulings]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134293903.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Syria's parliament voted to abolish a counter-terrorism court established in 2012. This court was reportedly used to prosecute thousands of anti-Assad Syrians on terrorism charges. The decision formalizes the court's abolition after new authorities treated it as defunct. The United Nations Human Rights Committee had raised concerns over judicial guarantees and fair trials. This vote occurred after opposition forces removed Bashar al-Assad from power in December 2024.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/syrias-parliament-votes-to-scrap-assad-era-terrorism-court-nullify-rulings/articleshow/134293903.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/syrias-parliament-votes-to-scrap-assad-era-terrorism-court-nullify-rulings/articleshow/134293903.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-16T23:21:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134294008,imgsize-104408.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Trump admin paid $9.5 billion to federal workers to stay home in 2025: Report]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134293631.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trump-admin-paid-9-5-billion-to-federal-workers-to-stay-home-in-2025-report/articleshow/134293631.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/trump-admin-paid-9-5-billion-to-federal-workers-to-stay-home-in-2025-report/articleshow/134293631.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-16T23:11:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134293807,imgsize-1203779.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2018, Matt Holliday paid $3M for Oklahoma land; his 62-acre estate now asks $9.8M]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134286974.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Former MLB star Matt Holliday's luxurious estate in Oklahoma has hit the market, boasting 62 acres of prime land including a private baseball field with professional-grade lighting. The stunning home, constructed in 2022, offers five spacious bedrooms and seven bathrooms. Among the standout features are a magnificent swimming pool and an indoor sports court. Originally listed for $12 million, it is now available for $9.8 million.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2018-matt-holliday-paid-3-million-for-oklahoma-land-years-later-his-62-acre-estate-with-a-baseball-field-and-2-million-pool-is-asking-9-8-million/articleshow/134286974.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2018-matt-holliday-paid-3-million-for-oklahoma-land-years-later-his-62-acre-estate-with-a-baseball-field-and-2-million-pool-is-asking-9-8-million/articleshow/134286974.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-17T02:55:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134287554,imgsize-1632491.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Anonymous donor gives Cincinnati $1.8 million for city’s biggest forest restoration in decades]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;marg